hadiths[99]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1401","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith, and in it was: ""For him is its double reward."""
"1402","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""When a slave is sincere to his master and worships his Lord in a good manner, then for him there is a double reward."""
"1403","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Verily, when a slave is sincere to his master and worships Allah in a good manner, then for him is a double reward."""
"1404","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When the time (of the Hour) draws very near, death will eliminate the best people of my Ummah just as one of you finishes the ripe, fresh dates from a bowl."""
"1405","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and he narrated this hadith."
"1406","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When a believer is afflicted with any hardship, it cleanses him of sins just as a furnace cleans iron of impurities."""
"1407","It is narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, when a servant becomes ill, Allah removes his sins during his illness just as a furnace removes impurities from iron."""
"1408","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""When Allah Almighty intends to implement His decision and decree, He takes away the intellects of the intelligent ones until He has carried out His decision and decree among them."""
"1409","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Illness is sufficient for well-being."""
"1410","Sayyiduna Ammar (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""Death is sufficient as an admonition, certainty is sufficient for the wealthy, and worship is sufficient for those who are occupied."""
"1411","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is sufficient for a man to be considered sinful that he neglects those whose sustenance he is responsible for."""
"1412","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is sufficient for a man . . . . "" and he narrated this hadith."
"1413","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""It is enough for a man to be considered sinful that he neglects those whom he is responsible for."""
"1414","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""It is enough for a man to be sinful that he says about his brother that which is found in him. So whoever says about his brother that which was found in him, then undoubtedly he has backbitten him, and whoever says about him that which was not in him, then undoubtedly he has eaten his (brother's) flesh."""
"1415","Sayyiduna Abu Umamah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is enough of a sin for a man that he relates everything he hears."""
"1416","Hafs bin Asim narrates from the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""It is enough of a sin for a man that he relates everything he hears."""
"1417","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is sufficient for a man’s good fortune that he is trusted in his religious and worldly affairs."""
"1418","Sayyiduna Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, while he was in Mina: ""Sometimes the one to whom a hadith is conveyed remembers it better than the one who heard it directly."""
"1419","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas‘ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said... and I have narrated it in brief."
"1420","This narration is also reported through another chain from Simak bin Harb with his chain in a similar manner."
"1421","Sayyiduna Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stood at the place of Khayf in Mina and said: “May Allah keep fresh and flourishing the person who hears my words, preserves them, and then conveys them to those who have not heard them. Sometimes the bearer of knowledge (fiqh) is not himself a faqih (jurist), and sometimes the bearer of knowledge conveys it to one who is more learned than himself.” And he narrated the complete hadith."
"1422","Sayyiduna Mu’adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: “May Allah keep fresh the person who hears my words and does not add anything to them. Sometimes the bearer of wisdom and knowledge conveys it to one who preserves it better than himself. There are three things in which a believer’s heart never betrays: acting sincerely for Allah, wishing well for the rulers, and adhering to the community of Muslims, for their supplication encompasses them from all sides.”"
"1423","Sayyiduna Ibn Jubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, who was among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), says that one day the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) felt intense hunger and tied a stone to his stomach. Then he said: ""Listen! How many souls there are who, in this world, eat and drink abundantly and live in luxury and comfort, but on the Day of Resurrection they will be hungry and naked. Listen! How many people there are who honor their own selves, while in reality they are humiliating them. Listen! How many people there are who humiliate their own selves, while (in reality) they are honoring them. Listen! How many there are who forcibly intrude into those things which Allah has granted to His Messenger as spoils (fay’), seeking luxury and comfort, while they have no share in them with Allah. Listen! Surely, the deeds of Paradise are surrounded by severe hardships. Listen! Surely, the deeds of Hell are surrounded by ease, pleasure, and desires. Listen! How many desires there are whose pleasure lasts but a moment, yet they become the cause of long-lasting sorrow."""
"1424","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How many are those who stand (in prayer) and gain nothing from their standing except staying awake at night, and how many are those who fast and gain nothing from their fasting except hunger and thirst."""
"1425","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""How many are those who stand (in prayer) and receive nothing from their standing except staying awake at night, and how many are those who fast and receive nothing from their fasting except hunger and thirst."""
"1426","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""How many fasting people are there who get nothing from their fast except hunger and thirst, and how many people who stand (in prayer at night) get nothing from their standing except staying awake at night."""
"1427","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""How many are there who eat food and give thanks, who surpass in reward those who fast and show patience."""
"1428","Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him) that he said: ""If the beggars did not lie, those who send them back empty-handed would never be safe from punishment."""
"1429","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew what I know, you would laugh little and weep much."""
"1430","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew what I know, you would weep more and laugh less."""
"1431","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you knew what I know, you would weep more and laugh less. And each of you would perform such a long prostration that his back would break, and would cry out so much that his voice would fade away. Weep, and if you cannot weep, then assume the appearance of one who is weeping."""
"1432","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) . . . . . and he narrated this hadith."
"1433","1433 - And narrated by Abu Muhammad ibn al-Nahhas, (he said): Ibn al-A’rabi narrated to us, Ibrahim (who is Ibn Fahd) narrated to us, Muslim narrated to us, Shu’bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, from Sulayman ibn Marthad, from Abu al-Darda’, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""And it was mentioned and narrated by Muslim ibn al-Hajjaj, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Shaybah, from Abdullah ibn Numayr, from Hisham ibn Urwah, from his father, from Aisha, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, in a long hadith, and in it: 'By Allah, if you knew what I know, you would weep much and laugh little.' ... the hadith."""
"1434","Sayyida Umayyah bint Sabiyyah Juhaniyyah (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If cattle knew death as the son of Adam knows it, you would not eat any fat animal."""
"1435","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while advising us said: ""If you were to see death and its swiftness, you would surely begin to hate hope and its deception."""
"1436","Sayyiduna Zayd bin Thabit (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you were to see death and its swiftness, you would surely begin to hate hope and its deception. There is no household whose Angel of Death does not check on them once every day. Then, when the appointed time of someone is complete, he seizes his soul, and the family members begin to weep and wail. So he (the Angel of Death) says: Why are you weeping and wailing? By Allah! I have neither decreased his lifespan for you nor withheld his sustenance; what is my sin? I am to return to you again and again."""
"1437","Sayyiduna Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""If a believer is even in a mouse hole, Allah Almighty will create something there to trouble him."""
"1438","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, if a believer were to be in any hole, Allah would still create for him something to cause him harm there."""
"1439","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If, in the sight of Allah, this world weighed even as much as the wing of a mosquito, He would not grant a disbeliever even a sip of water from it."""
"1440","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If, in the sight of Allah, this world had the value of even a mosquito's wing, He would not have granted a disbeliever even a sip of water from it."""
"1441","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, if the son of Adam were to possess two valleys full of wealth, he would certainly seek a third valley along with them, and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except the dust (of the grave), and Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents."""
"1442","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Waqqad Al-Laithi, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has said: Indeed, We have sent down wealth for the establishment of prayer and the giving of zakat. If the son of Adam possesses a valley (full of wealth), he will wish that he had two valleys, and if he has two valleys, he will wish that he had a third with them. And nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except the dust (of the grave), and Allah accepts the repentance of whoever repents."""
"1443","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, if the son of Adam has two valleys of wealth, he will certainly seek a third as well."" The remaining text is the same as that of the other hadith. And Muslim has also narrated it with his chain from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) in a marfu‘ form: If the son of Adam has two valleys of wealth, he will certainly seek a third as well."
"1444","Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""If you truly put your trust in Allah as He deserves to be trusted, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds: they go out hungry in the morning and return full in the evening."""
"1445","Sayyiduna Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""If you truly put your trust in Allah as He deserves to be trusted... and he narrated this hadith."""
"1446","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you did not commit sins, Allah would bring a people who would commit sins, then He would forgive them and admit them into Paradise."""
"1447","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""If you did not commit sins, I would fear for you something even more severe than that (the consequence of sin), and that is pride and arrogance."""
"1448","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has said: I am as My servant thinks of Me, and I am with him when he remembers Me."""
"1449","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: ""Allah Almighty has said that My love has become obligatory for those who love each other for My sake and visit each other for My sake."""
"1450","Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty has said . . . . . . . . and he narrated this hadith in a brief form."""
"1451","Sayyiduna Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: «لا إلٰه إلا الله» is My fortress; whoever enters it will be safe from My punishment."""
"1452","Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I become extremely angry at the person who oppresses someone who finds no helper besides me."" Al-Tabarani said: Only Sharik narrated it from Abu Ishaq, and in narrating it, Mas'ar is unique."
"1453","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: O world! Be bitter for My friends, do not be sweet for them, otherwise you will put them into trial."""
"1454","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says to the world: O world! Be a servant to the one who becomes My servant, and O world! Weary the one who becomes your servant."""
"1455","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, says: Whoever is kept busy with My remembrance from asking Me, I will give him better than what I give to those who ask."""
"1456","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who narrates from Jibril (peace be upon him), who narrates from Allah the Blessed and Exalted, that Allah the Blessed and Exalted says: ""Whoever shows disrespect to any of My friends, then surely he has openly invited Me to war, and I do not hesitate in anything that I am going to do as much as I hesitate in seizing the soul of My believing servant (because) he dislikes death (due to the pain of the body), and I also dislike causing him pain, but there is no alternative for him other than this."""
"1457","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""Allah, the Blessed and Exalted, said: Whoever harms any of My friends has made lawful what I have forbidden, and no servant has attained nearness to Me through anything more beloved to Me than the obligations I have enjoined upon him. And indeed, My servant continues to draw near to Me through voluntary acts until I love him. (Then) if he calls upon Me, I answer him, and if he asks of Me, I grant him. And I do not hesitate regarding anything I am to do as I hesitate regarding the soul of My servant, for he dislikes death (due to the pain of the body), and I dislike to harm him."""
"1458","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, Allah, the Exalted, spoke to Musa (peace be upon him) with one hundred and forty thousand words, all of which were admonitions. Among what was said in that conversation was: O Musa! Truly, those who pretend and affect asceticism for My sake have not pretended anything in this world like asceticism, and those who seek nearness have not attained nearness like abstaining from what I have made unlawful, and those who worship have not worshipped like the worship of weeping out of fear of Me.” This hadith is concise."
"1459","It is narrated from Jubair through another chain that he said: ""O Musa! Indeed, those who pretend and affectation have not shown any affectation in the world like that of asceticism, and those who seek nearness have not attained nearness like that of abstaining and avoiding what I have forbidden, and those who worship have not worshipped like the worship of weeping out of My fear."""
"1460","It is narrated from Juwaybir with another chain: ""The reality is that those who feign and affectation have not feigned anything in the world like the asceticism they feign, and those who seek nearness have not attained nearness like that attained by abstaining from and avoiding what I have forbidden, and the worshippers have not worshipped like the worship of weeping out of My fear."""
"1461","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Jibril (peace be upon him) said that Allah Almighty says: I have chosen this religion for Myself, and nothing can keep it upright except generosity and good character, so honor and dignify it through both of them as long as you remain with it.”"
"1462","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), who narrates from Jibril (peace be upon him), who narrates from Allah the Blessed and Exalted, that Allah said: ""When I send any calamity upon any of My servants in his body, wealth, or children, and then he receives it with beautiful patience, I feel shy on the Day of Resurrection to set up the scales for him or to open the record of deeds for him."""
"1463","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Allah Almighty says: Grandeur is My cloak and greatness is My lower garment, so whoever tries to take any one of them from Me, I will throw him into the Fire."""
"1464","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Prophet (peace be upon him), who narrates from his Lord, the Exalted, that He said: ""Majesty is My lower garment and greatness is My cloak, so whoever tries to snatch any one of them from Me, I will throw him into Hell."""
"1465","Sufyan narrated this tradition once as a marfu’ (attributed) to the Prophet (peace be upon him) and once as mawquf (stopped) at Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): “Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, said: ‘Grandeur is My cloak and greatness is My lower garment, so whoever tries to snatch any of these from Me, I will throw him into the Fire.’”"
"1466","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that among the supplications of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was this: ""O Allah! Indeed, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is of no benefit, from a heart that does not fear, from a supplication that is not accepted, and from a soul that is never satisfied. I seek refuge in You from the evil of these four things."""
"1467","This narration is also reported through another chain from Khulaf bin Khalifah with his chain, and at its end it is: ""O Allah! Indeed, I seek refuge in You from the evil of these four things."""
"1468","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""O Allah! Indeed, I seek refuge in You from knowledge that is of no benefit, from deeds that do not ascend to Your presence, from a heart that does not fear (You), and from a supplication that is not heard."""
"1469","Sayyida Umm Salama (may Allah be pleased with her) says that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) left my house, he would raise his gaze towards the sky and recite this supplication: ""O Allah! Indeed, I seek refuge in You from going astray or being led astray, from slipping or being made to slip, from doing wrong or having wrong done to me, from acting ignorantly or having ignorance shown to me."""
"1470","Yusuf bin Atiyyah reports that Abdul Hakam bin Maimoon came to visit me during my illness, and he informed me that he went with Thabit to Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and he narrated this hadith to them: Indeed, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was suffering from some ailment, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to him: ""Say: O Allah! Indeed, I ask You for Your swift recovery, patience upon Your trial, and to depart from this world towards Your mercy."""
"1471","Lady Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, narrates from our master Abu Bakr Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, that indeed the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to supplicate with this prayer: ""O Allah! Ordain goodness for me and choose only goodness for me."""
"1472","Sayyiduna Abu Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him), who participated in Badr, says that the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to say: “O Allah! You have made my appearance good, so make my character good as well.”"
"1473","Sayyiduna Ibn Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: ""O Allah! You have made my appearance good, so make my character good as well."""
"1474","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): Tell me, if I come to know which night is Laylat al-Qadr, what supplication should I make? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You should say: O Allah! Indeed, You are Forgiving, You love forgiveness, so forgive me."""
"1475","This narration is also reported through another chain from Jariri with their chain in the same manner."
"1476","It is narrated from Sayyida Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: O Messenger of Allah! The month of Ramadan has arrived, so which supplication should I recite? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You should say: O Allah! Indeed, You are Forgiving, You love to forgive, so forgive me."""
"1477","It is narrated from Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: O Messenger of Allah! Tell me, if I find the Night of Qadr, which supplication should I recite in it? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You should say: O Allah! Indeed, You are Forgiving, You love forgiveness, so forgive me."""
"1478","Sayyidah Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I asked: O Messenger of Allah! If I find the Night of Qadr, which supplication should I recite in it? He (peace be upon him) said: ""You should say: O Allah! Indeed, You are Forgiving, You love to forgive, so forgive me."""
"1479","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that one of the supplications of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was: ""O Allah! Forgive my sins which I committed by mistake and those I committed deliberately, those I committed secretly and those I committed openly, those I committed unknowingly and those I committed knowingly."""
"1480","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husayn (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that Husayn, before accepting Islam, came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: Muhammad (peace be upon him)! Abdul Muttalib was better for his people; he used to feed them the liver and hump meat (of animals), whereas you slaughter these (animals) completely. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) replied as Allah willed. Then Husayn said: Muhammad (peace be upon him)! What do you command me to recite? He (peace be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Indeed, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul, and I ask You to grant me steadfastness in my good deeds."" He (Imran) says: After that, Husayn accepted Islam, then came to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: Indeed, I asked you the first time, and now again I ask you, what do you command me to recite? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Say: ""O Allah! Forgive my sins which I committed secretly and openly, those I committed by mistake and those I committed deliberately, those I committed unknowingly and those I committed knowingly."""
"1481","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Indeed, successful is the one who purifies it.” ( al-Shams: 9) And the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “O Allah! Grant my soul its piety and purify it, for You are the best to purify it. You are its Guardian and Master.” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was in prayer at that time."
"1482","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed, when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) feared a people, he would supplicate as follows: ""O Allah! Indeed, I seek refuge in You from their evils, and I present You against them."""
"1483","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Suhaib (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was moving his lips during the days of Khaybar. He was asked, ""What supplication are you making?"" He replied: ""I am saying: (O Allah!) I walk and move about only with Your help, I fight only with Your help, and I attack only with Your help."""
"1484","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! Protect as Walid protects."""
"1485","This narration is also reported through another chain from Abdul Wahab bin Duhak with his chain in the same manner."
"1486","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! Protect as Walid protected."""
"1487","Salim narrates from his father that indeed the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Indeed, I ask You for protection as Walid sought protection."""
"1488","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he used to supplicate: ""O Allah! (At Badr and Ahzab) You made the former people of Quraysh taste punishment, so now bestow favor and honor upon those who came after them."""
"1489","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that never ask a blind person for a need, and never ask for a need at night, and when you have to ask for a need, turn towards that person with your face, because modesty is in both eyes. And go out for your need in the morning, because the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Bless my Ummah in its morning time."""
"1490","Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Bless my Ummah in its early morning."""
"1491","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sakhr Ghamidi (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said this statement."
"1492","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) saying: ""O Allah! Bless my Ummah in its Thursday morning."""
"1493","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Sakhr Ghamidi (may Allah be pleased with him) that indeed the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Bless my Ummah in its early morning."""
"1494","Sayyiduna Nabit bin Shurit (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Allah! Bless my Ummah in its early morning."" Al-Tabarani said: This hadith is narrated from Nabit only with this chain, and his son is unique in narrating it from him."
"1495","Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""O Possessor of well-being! All desires end with You."""
"1496","Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that among the supplications of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was this: ""O Lord! Accept my repentance, wash away my sins, and accept my supplication."""
"1497","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that whenever the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) intended to set out on a journey, before rising from his place, he would certainly recite these words: “O Allah! I rise with Your help, turn towards You, and hold firmly to You. Upon You is my trust and in You is my hope. O Allah! Be sufficient for me in my important and unimportant matters, and also in those which You know better than I do. O Allah! Grant me the provision of piety, forgive my sins, and wherever I turn, direct me towards goodness.” The narrator says that then he (having recited these words) would set out for the journey."
"1498","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! Indeed, I ask You for a balanced life, a pure death, and an end in which there is no disgrace or humiliation."""
"1499","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to supplicate: ""O Allah! Indeed, I ask You for a pure life, an easy death, and an end in which there is no disgrace or humiliation."""
